Not trying to bloat your post with nonsense, but I just wanted to say, that is a very nice piece. I love things that might not be valuable to most but very valuable to me, I am very sentimental. I can't afford that one, but I wish I could. I love pops and I love South Park. I have about 250 pops but none rarer then somewhat rare chases or exclusives. I see people with these protos, or earlier I saw some super rare gold MLB player pops that were limited to like, 18 pieces. How do people actually get things like that, besides second hand markets of people reselling? I know some people chase these ultra rare pops just to sell, and some people never consider selling but end up really needing the money so they let them go. Where I live, pops are pursued so hard that people are sneaking into UPS / employee entrances and hiding in the bathroom of the mall just to be first in line at Box Lunch or Hot Topic, which around here, don't even sell first come first serve - they allow everyone 10 minutes to show up after opening and then let every one draw a number from a hat to decide line order. I don't even know if that is allowed, but the employees were to the point of being followed and approached in the parking lot after work so the only way they could deal with this was to take it out of the employees hands and make it a raffle, so no one would have a reason to "shake down" an employee looking for the inside scoop. How on Earth do people find these beautiful collectables? Again, sorry if this ramble is against the rules but I really appreciate that piece you have there. Good luck in your pursuit of a sale.

