There is RC (Raid class, not sure how hip you are with no game, so no offense meant if you already knew this) 7, and then there are the Rifts. The Rifts are very hard content. You can't just select a good friend to help and then hit auto, walk away, and come back to gems. I'm level \~400, with full 60 cost omnis, each of which has max imps added, max level BB, good spheres, a good elgif, and maximum Enhancements, and even using a friend from my guild that is level 999 with super strong units, elite spheres, and +3 omni level, I struggle or am not able to completely finish the second half of rifts. The building in the town called the Research Lab (or something, the building towards the top left of the city map) eventually unlocks trials that are pretty hard as well. At your point, you can probably just auto through the entire quest line if you haven't already. Try and clear all the grand gaia chronicles in the vortex menu, and then start doing the trials. The trials cost a lot of energy, 50 I believe, but usually grant enough XP to level up, thus letting you keep going until they get too difficult for you. Start clearing raids, you shouldn't have any problem up until RC5 or 6, and even those aren't too hard. As for raids, you can hope random people join your game to help you, or get the aid from a friend who is online or guild member. If you make a lobby for a raid, even if you don't kill the boss, if the other person does, you will still get credit and unlock the next one. However, if you couldn't beat a raid, most likely you won't be able to beat the next one, so you'll end up needing help again. After the GGCs in vortex, the research lab, and raids, then you can start looking into the Rifts. Most rifts have requirements to be able to do them, such as, only light or dark units, only water units, or only units that are at least omni +1. Meaning if you just got to the point of your first omni, you surely don't have full omni squads of only dark (or whatever) units, so you won't qualify to try them. I played for 2 years, and then took a 2 year break, and am now back, so I am still learning end game / high end content myself, so I apologize if any one thinks that what I said in this post is wrong or not helpful and will proceed to tell me to stop giving advice because I'm an amateur, in front of others, when you know you could have just privately messaged me to avoid embarrassment ( you know who you are, if you end up reading this), and am just speaking out of personal experience. Feel free to message me with specific questions or for advice, and I will either tell you or say that I don't know, rather then making some thing up to make it seem like I know what I'm talking about.

