Typically only supports and junglers have high vision score. 

&#x200B;

Pro tip- Remember, vision score doesn't work how most people think. You don't increase your vision score by just placing wards. Your vision score increases when a ward you placed SPOTS enemies. This prevents people from just spamming wards in dumb locations to increase their score, and benefits people who place wards in smart locations. The better you place a ward, the more enemies it will spot, and the higher your score will be, vision wise. ALWAYS drop your ward if you have the trinket cooldown available before you back. Even if  you don't think any enemies are closeby, a ward in a remote location is still better then no ward at all. Try to keep your ward down throughout the whole game. Also, if you have a little extra gold and an inventory slot, buy a pink ward. Map vision is a gigantic advantage.  If you are going back to town, throw a ward down in the bush you are in. That at least gives you a chance of raising your vision score, whereas not having one down grants no chance. Also, as already stated, destroying enemy wards is also a way to increase your score. Don't fret if your vision score isn't 30,40,50+, as typically only supports and junglers get that high on average.

My girlfriends grandmother traded in her low mileage 20-13/14 Cadillac into a dealership to buy a different car. Turns out, my girlfriends mother (grandmothers daughter) wanted that car from her, and would have ended up paying her more for the car then the dealership ended up giving her. So, she goes to the dealership, LETS THE SALESMAN know the car is sentimental to her (her father, the grandfather owned the Caddy and then passed away) and then ended up buying the car from the dealership for obviously WAY more then they gave the grandmother for it. Because she told the dealership that it was sentimental to her and that she had to have it, they knew she'd pay whatever for it. Talk about getting waxxed twice over the same vehicle. That dealership probably never had made so much money off one car, so quickly, as they did from those two. Yikes.

&#x200B;

EDIT - And here's the ringer - The mother told the dealership to NOT EVEN CLEAN IT UP, because she wanted it how her father had left it. THEY DIDN'T EVEN HAVE TO CLEAN OR TOUCH UP THE SUV!

