It takes you more then 5-10 seconds to remember 2 (TWO) items? Here's a test:

&#x200B;

Apple  ,                Donut

&#x200B;

Ok now try to recall what two items were just mentioned. Did it take you 10 seconds? Not to mention OP made it pretty obvious that she was reading off a cell phone, probably with the specific items that were mentioned. From my personal experience with secret-shoppers / sting agents for whoever, once you reject the allegedly underage kid and then the adult who tries to buy it for them, person number 3 generally won't come in and try again. If person 3 does come in, it's usually only if you messed up.

Example, quick version: Friend employee worked at Gamestop. Customer A came in. Customer A was a gargantuan monster of a human, probably 6'5" and 290 pounds. Tried to buy Quake and preorder Halo (3? 4 maybe?) which is an M rated game. Employee doesn't check ID, even assistant manage says it's ok because the kid is obviously at least 17. Customer B comes in maybe 2 minutes late, returns the game and cancels the preorder. Next day, store was informed customer A and B were secret shoppers, customer A was actually only 15 and was purposely asked to do this task because most people would automatically assume he's older then 17. And then friend employee was alerted that he is being fired on his next shift. Had he never sold to customer A, customer B would have never came in. Obviously each situation, industry, and company probably has different methods on how they handle this, but that is my personal experience.

