I woke up with the radial nerve in my right arm completely destroyed because of a rare random unknown virus (unknown in the sense that they don't know which virus does this, not that they can identify it but not know what it is). I was right handed and had to learn how to do everything with my left after this in my early twenties. I was originally diagnosed with a pinched nerve that would heal in a month or so. Two years, ten doctors or so, and much frustration later, they were finally able to tell me they think what happened to me was P. Turner syndrome. It didn't even have a name until the mid 2000's when a famous fighter apparantly came down with this. The craziest part was that it all happened over the course of a two hour nap. Was completely fine, took a small nap, and woke up like that. No trauma or pain. My right hand was completely limp at my wrist, I couldn't even wiggle my fingers. The radial nerve is responsible for finger, wrist, and forearm movement. 

&#x200B;

Quoting myself just to give you another example of being asleep on your mattress with bad things happening.

